  "read": "2026-10-05",
  "method": "Depth pass adding more models for footwear brands that had only 1-2 products in research-clothing-sneakers-a.json and research-clothing-sneakers-b.json (Saucony, Converse) and in other research-clothing-*.json files (Charly, Panam, UGG, Crocs, Sorel, Blundstone, Timberland, Dr. Martens, ECCO, Geox), with emphasis on CA, IE and MX markets. Mix of direct page fetches (WebFetch) of saucony.com, converse.ca and panam.com.mx, and WebSearch result snippets that quoted an exact price from the cited domain (brand site or, where noted, a named retailer) when a direct fetch returned 403/404/parse errors (converse.com, charly.com, ugg.com/ca and /mx, crocs.ca/.com.mx/.co.uk, sorelfootwear.ca, blundstone.ca/.com, drmartens.com/ca and the EU site, gb.ecco.com, geox.com GB). Checked existing research-clothing*.json files first for brand/name overlap; dropped would-be duplicates (a Blundstone 550 Walnut CA entry already present in research-clothing-shoes-2.json) and skipped brands that already had 4+ entries per the user's own 1-2-count criterion (Clarks, Cole Haan, Sam Edelman).",
  "dropped": [
   "Blundstone 550 Walnut, CA: dropped as a duplicate of the '550 - Classics, Walnut' entry already in research-clothing-shoes-2.json; used a US-market 550 entry instead.",
   "UGG Tasman Slipper (men's and women's), GB: dropped because the brand's own product name uses the word 'Slipper', which is not one of the required footwear words (Sneaker/Trainer/Running Shoe/Boot/Sandal/Loafer/Shoe/Tenis); used Classic Short II Boot (CA) and Classic Mini II Boot (MX) instead, both of which use 'Boot'.",
   "Sam Edelman Hazel loafer, CA: no Nordstrom.ca or samedelman.ca price page or snippet in CAD surfaced; dropped rather than guess a conversion.",
   "Clarks and Cole Haan: both already have 4+ entries across other research-clothing-*.json files, so neither meets the 1-2-count criterion this pass targets; no new entries added for either."
  ]
 },
